1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,870
What if the ground beneath one country

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:07,214
held almost three quarters of a mineral the whole world needs?

3
00:00:07,664 --> 00:00:10,948
This is Türkiye. And that mineral is boron,

4
00:00:11,228 --> 00:00:17,394
found in glass, powerful magnets and even nuclear shielding.

5
00:00:17,674 --> 00:00:22,398
Türkiye holds about seventy-three percent of the world's reserves.

6
00:00:22,848 --> 00:00:24,496
Then there's stone.

7
00:00:24,776 --> 00:00:29,519
Around forty percent of the world's natural stone reserves are here,

8
00:00:29,799 --> 00:00:32,304
including the marble the Romans carved.

9
00:00:32,754 --> 00:00:34,834
Deep under the Black Sea,

10
00:00:35,114 --> 00:00:41,576
Türkiye found an estimated seven hundred eighty-five billion cubic meters of natural gas.

11
00:00:42,026 --> 00:00:49,774
And in Eskişehir, officials say they found six hundred ninety-four million tons of rare earth ore,

12
00:00:50,054 --> 00:00:53,983
the elements inside wind turbines and electric motors.

13
00:00:54,433 --> 00:01:02,800
Altogether, the industry estimates Türkiye's untapped underground wealth at three point five trillion dollars.

14
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:04,693
The real question is:

15
00:01:04,973 --> 00:01:07,408
who will turn it into technology?
